---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy | Friends of Lake Henry";
const description =
    "Learn what information Friends of Lake Henry collects, how it’s used, and how we protect it.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
    <div class="container" style="--maxw: 900px;">
        <section class="card shade-reference enter-block" style="margin-top: var(--section-gap);">
            <div class="panel privacyContent">
                <h1 class="h1-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
                <p class="lead">
                    Friends of Lake Henry (“we,” “our,” or “us”) is committed to protecting your privacy.
                    This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and how we protect it.
                    By using our website or providing information to us, you agree to this Privacy Policy.
                </p>

                <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

                <h3>1. Contact Requests</h3>
                <p>
                    When you submit the contact form on our website, we collect your name, email address, and the message you provide
                    so we can respond to your inquiry.
                </p>

                <h3>2. Photo Submissions</h3>
                <p>If you submit a photo through our website, we collect:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>The uploaded image</li>
                    <li>Optional title and caption</li>
                    <li>Required alternative (alt) text for accessibility</li>
                    <li>An optional “submitted by” name</li>
                    <li>A category selected during submission</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Submitted photos are reviewed before being published to the public photo gallery.</p>

                <h3>3. Facebook Page and Raffle Information</h3>
                <p>
                    We use our organization’s Facebook Page integration to find drawing videos and winner announcements
                    for the raffle website. This may involve reading public Page post text, publication dates,
                    post and video identifiers, video availability information, and announcement images.
                    Visitors do not need to sign in with Facebook to use this website.
                </p>
                <p>
                    We process winner-announcement images to identify information such as winner names, hometowns,
                    ticket numbers, and prize details. Results that pass our automated checks may be published on the
                    raffle page; uncertain or conflicting results are held for administrator review. We also keep
                    related processing records to support review and prevent duplicate entries.
                </p>

                <h3>4. Technical and Security Information</h3>
                <p>
                    To protect the website and prevent spam or abuse, we process limited technical information, including IP address
                    and request metadata. This information is used for security, rate limiting, and abuse prevention and is not used
                    for advertising or tracking visitors across sites.
                </p>

                <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
                <p>We use the information we collect only for the following purposes:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Responding to contact requests</strong> (replying to messages submitted through the contact form)</li>
                    <li><strong>Reviewing and publishing photo submissions</strong> (reviewing and, if approved, displaying photos in the public gallery)</li>
                    <li><strong>Reporting raffle drawings and results</strong> (finding official Page videos and processing and verifying winner announcements)</li>
                    <li><strong>Maintaining site security</strong> (detecting and preventing spam, automated submissions, and abusive behavior)</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information and do <strong>not</strong> use it for advertising or marketing.
                </p>

                <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

                <h3>Cloudflare (Hosting and Security)</h3>
                <p>
                    Our website is delivered and protected by Cloudflare. Cloudflare may process IP addresses and set security-related
                    cookies that are required to protect the site from malicious traffic.
                </p>

                <h3>Cloudflare Turnstile (Spam Prevention)</h3>
                <p>
                    We use Cloudflare Turnstile on certain forms to distinguish real users from automated abuse.
                    Turnstile may process IP address and related request data as part of this security function.
                </p>

                <h3>Resend (Email Delivery)</h3>
                <p>
                    When you submit the contact form, your name, email address, and message are sent via Resend so the message can be
                    delivered to us by email.
                </p>

                <h3>Cloudflare (Winner-Photo Processing)</h3>
                <p>
                    We use Cloudflare’s hosted AI processing to read public Facebook winner-announcement images and
                    extract raffle results. The images can contain personal information, including names and hometowns.
                    Automated extraction is subject to verification checks and administrator review when results are uncertain.
                </p>

                <h3>Facebook (Page Integration and Embedded Video Content)</h3>
                <p>
                    We read public content from our Facebook Page to support raffle video discovery and winner-photo
                    processing, as described above. Deleting information from our website does not delete the original
                    Facebook content or information in a Facebook account.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Some pages of the site embed Facebook video content (such as Facebook Live or Reels) using Facebook’s official embed player.
                    When you view embedded Facebook content, Facebook may collect information and set cookies or similar technologies according to
                    its own policies. This may occur even if you do not have a Facebook account or are not logged in. We do not control how
                    Facebook processes this data.
                </p>

                <h2>Cookies and Tracking</h2>
                <p>We do not use analytics or advertising cookies on this website.</p>
                <p>However, certain third-party services used on the site may set cookies or use similar technologies, including:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Cloudflare may set necessary security cookies to protect the site.</li>
                    <li>Facebook embedded content may set cookies or collect data when the embed is loaded and viewed.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Data Retention</h2>
                <p>
                    We retain personal information only for as long as necessary to respond to inquiries, review and manage submitted
                    content, report and review raffle results, maintain site security, and comply with applicable legal,
                    raffle, or administrative obligations. Some records may need to be retained when those obligations apply.
                </p>

                <h2>Data Security</h2>
                <p>
                    We take reasonable measures to protect your information, including the use of encrypted connections (HTTPS) and
                    restricted access to administrative systems. No online service can be guaranteed to be completely secure, and you
                    provide information at your own risk.
                </p>

                <h2>Your Rights and Choices</h2>
                <p>You may request:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Access to or correction of your submitted information</li>
                    <li>Deletion of contact submissions, submitted photos, or Facebook-derived raffle information associated with you, where applicable and legally permitted</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    To request deletion, follow our <a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion Instructions</a> and email
                    <a href="mailto:friendsoflakehenryblair@gmail.com?subject=Data%20Deletion%20Request">friendsoflakehenryblair@<wbr />gmail.com</a>
                    with the subject <strong>Data Deletion Request</strong>, identifying the information you want deleted.
                    We may request reasonable verification of your identity or authority before acting on the request.
                    Other privacy questions can also be sent to this email address.
                </p>

                <h2>Children’s Privacy</h2>
                <p>
                    This website is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children under 13.
                    We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
                </p>

                <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
                <p>
                    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any updates will be posted on this page with a revised
                    effective date. Continued use of the site indicates acceptance of the updated policy.
                </p>

                <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
                    Last updated: November 3, 2026
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .privacyContent {
        background: var(--shade-reference);
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .privacyContent a {
        color: #b9dcff;
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: .18em;
    }

    .privacyContent a:focus-visible {
        outline: 2px solid currentColor;
        outline-offset: 3px;
    }
</style>
